  "interpretation": "MIXED pattern supporting primarily attenuation with axis-dependent divergence component. Verbosity: concordance 71-85% across all 4 judges (mean 77.5%) with significant correlations (r=0.26-0.39, all p<.02) → consistent with attenuation (Likert direction is correct but magnitude compressed). Formality: concordance is judge-dependent — Llama-70B 83% (attenuation), but GPT-4o 53% and Qwen3 53% (near-chance, suggesting partial construct divergence). Formality correlations are also judge-split: Llama-70B r=0.35 p<.001 and Gemini r=0.26 p=.015 (significant), but GPT-4o r=0.12 p=.26 and Qwen3 r=0.04 p=.71 (NS). Bias-corrected ORs show negligible shrinkage (0.4-2.5%), confirming raw ORs are robust at n≈85. Bottom line: the blindspot is predominantly attenuation (especially for verbosity), but formality shows a judge-dependent divergence component where some judges' Likert rankings disagree with their own pairwise preferences at item level.",
  "methodology_notes": {
    "nli_filter": "nli_cf >= 0.90 applied to both scored and pairwise data",
    "pairwise_tie_handling": "Inconsistent pairwise trials (trial1 != trial2) excluded from concordance denominator; scored as 0.5 in correlation",
    "concordance_ci": "Wilson score interval at 95%",
    "correlation_method": "Pearson r + Spearman rho (both reported, Pearson primary)",
    "bias_correction": "Nemes (2009) log(OR)*(n-1)/n + Hedges (1981) J=1-3/(4df-1)",
    "gpt4o_formality_pairwise_note": "pairwise_results_32b.jsonl is the GPT-4o formality pairwise file (naming artifact from early experiments); confirmed 100% ID overlap with scored.jsonl"
